Loams Desktop agent daemon (loams-agentd)
Copyright 2026 The Loams Authors

This directory's crate and the other crates/loams-agentd* crates are Loams
Desktop's per-user agent daemon (docs/design/50-loams-desktop-daemon.md).

Zeron
-----
The daemon derives from Zeron (https://github.com/zeronsh/zeron):

  MIT License
  Copyright (c) 2026 Wing

The full licence text is in LICENSE, kept unmodified. Do not remove it.

The loams-agentd* crates whose Cargo.toml sets `license = "MIT"` derive from
Zeron. They came through the Loams Desktop fork
(https://github.com/ostrium-labs/loams-desktop), which keeps Zeron's history,
at the commit recorded as `source_commit` in import-provenance.json
(c9205f8f949711c3315af551c804c56452d2fbd7). Those crates, and the Loams
Authors' changes to them, are under the MIT License in LICENSE.

The other loams-agentd* crates are licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0, like the rest of this repository (see the root LICENSE):
- loams-agentd-link, written by the Loams Authors in the fork (its own
  LICENSE);
- the crates that are new in this repository.

README.md lists each crate's licence and origin. The workspace test
`licence_fields_are_set` keeps the Cargo.toml fields in step with that table.

The Loams identity strings in loams-agentd-proto (src/brand.rs) came from the
fork's Apache-2.0 loams-desktop-brand crate, which the Loams Authors wrote.
The Loams Authors place those lines under loams-agentd-proto's MIT License.

"Zeron" names the upstream project and is used here only to say where this
code comes from. "Loams", "Loams Desktop" and "loams-agentd" name this
software.

Other notices in this directory
-------------------------------
- SCOPED_NOTICE.md is the notice written when the fork was imported into
  apps/desktop/native. It is kept for history; the import's paths are now
  crates/loams-agentd*.
- THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md began as Zeron's third-party notice. It covered
  the tree-sitter grammars, GPUI and the gpui-component fork, the Symbols
  icons, fonts, and the voice model. All of those belonged to crates that
  were deleted, so none of them is built into or shipped with loams-agentd,
  and their entries were removed. The imported text is at
  `git show 6e470a96^:apps/desktop/native/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`. A bundled
  third-party asset added later is listed there.

Third-party components the fork added
-------------------------------------
loams-agentd-link links:
- connect-rust (`connectrpc`), Apache-2.0,
  https://github.com/connectrpc/connect-rust
- buffa (`buffa`, `buffa-types`), Apache-2.0,
  https://github.com/anthropics/buffa
- keyring, MIT OR Apache-2.0,
  https://github.com/open-source-cooperative/keyring-rs
- webbrowser, MIT OR Apache-2.0, https://github.com/amodm/webbrowser-rs

Other Rust dependencies are pinned in the root Cargo.lock. Each keeps its
own licence, and `cargo deny check licenses` (deny.toml) checks them.
